course: dictionary
lesson: 11482
title: Affixes and the word affix
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An affix is a small group of letters added to a word to change its meaning. Added to the front, it is a prefix, like un- in «unhappy», which means not happy. Added to the end, it is a suffix, like -ness in «kindness», which turns kind into the idea of being kind.
explain: Affix is also a verb. It means to stick, fix or attach something to something else. «Affix a stamp to the envelope» tells you to stick the stamp on. Forms and instructions use this word often, so it helps to know it.
explain: The same spelling can do two jobs. As a noun, an affix is the letter group itself. As a verb, to affix is the action of attaching. Read the sentence to see which one you have.
fact: An affix is a letter group added to a word to change its meaning.
fact: A prefix goes at the start of a word, like un- or re-.
fact: A suffix goes at the end of a word, like -ful or -ness.
fact: «Affix» as a verb means to stick, fix or attach something to something else.
fact: Phrases you may see are «affix a label» and «affix a photo».
exercise: What is a prefix? | A sound made by a letter | A letter group added to the end of a word | A word that means very old | *A letter group added to the start of a word
exercise: «Affix a stamp to the envelope.» What does affix mean here? | To read aloud | To wash | To tear off | *To stick on
exercise: Which word has the suffix -ful? | rewrite | unhappy | cold | *hopeful
test: «Reheat the soup before lunch.» What does the prefix re- add to heat? | *Again | Not | Very | Before
test: «Please affix your photo to the form.» What should you do? | *Stick your photo onto the form | Post the form to a friend | Draw a picture on the form | Tear the photo up
exam: «The label was affixed to the box.» What does affixed mean? | Torn off | Painted over | Read aloud | *Stuck on
